{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"source": "data\\documents\\csv\\QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "filename": "QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "filepath": "data\\documents\\csv\\QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "page": 9, "title": "QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "year": "2024", "row": 8}, "page_content": "\ufeffWhat is psoriasis and what are its common symptoms?: What are the recommended medications for acne treatment?\nPsoriasis is a chronic autoimmune condition that results in the overproduction of skin cells. This overproduction leads to patches of thick, red skin covered with silvery scales. Common symptoms include red patches of skin covered with thick, silvery scales, small scaling spots (commonly seen in children), dry and cracked skin that may bleed, itching, burning, or soreness, thickened, pitted, or ridged nails, and swollen and stiff joints.: The type of medication your doctor prescribes for your acne depends on your symptoms and the severity of your condition. Commonly recommended medications include:\r\n\r\n1. Topical retinoids: These are derived from vitamin A and include drugs like tretinoin, adapalene, and tazarotene.\r\n2. Antibiotics: These can be applied to the skin or taken orally to reduce bacteria and inflammation.\r\n3. Salicylic acid and azelaic acid: These help prevent pores from becoming blocked.\r\n4. Dapsone: This is a topical gel especially beneficial for inflammatory acne.\r\n5. Oral contraceptives: These can help regulate hormones that cause acne in women.", "type": "Document"}}